!! GasChemicalMechanism.in - SAPRC07TC, Williams case
!! ASP
!! Translated from the CMAQ mechanism definition mech_saprc07tc_ae6_aq.def by CB6r5Translation/mech2asp.py
!! (see CB6r5Translation/NewMechanisms_README.md for every choice and warning).
!! Gas-phase core plus CMAQ AERO organic-aerosol chemistry (AE group SOA yields -> SVAVB / SVBNZ / SVXYL / SVTOL ..., SOAALK, pcSOA).
!! SOA counters (ISOPRXN, TRPRXN, SESQRXN, ALKRXN, XYLNRXN ...) are replaced by their CMAQ mass-yield products; MTNO3 / ISOPNN are
!! partitioning vapors (see cmaq_ae.py, OrgPhaseChems.in, OrganicDissolution.in).  NOT translated: chlorine, heterogeneous (IEPOX,
!! glyoxal) uptake, particle-phase hydrolysis / oligomerisation (OLIG_*, HYD_*), toxics.
!! translated.  598 CMAQ statements -> 597 ASP reactions.
!! REQUIRES common_asp >= c506969 (1-body rate flags 18-21 for the CMAQ heterogeneous chemistry and OrgPhaseReactions.in 53d416e; 1-body rate flag 13, 3-body flag 4 and the earlier flag fixes 40c1760 are older)
!! (2-body flag 5 = 508ba8d, 3-body flag 2 = f3f1107).
!! Rate-flag conventions: see the header of the baseline decks; new flags:
!!   1-body flag 13:  k = kf / Keq,  kf = fall-off with explicit Troe N
!!       13; A0; n0; E0; Ai; ni; Ei; F; N; KeqA; KeqE;   k0 = A0 (T/300)^-n0 exp(E0/T) [M],  ki likewise,  Keq = KeqA exp(KeqE/T)
!!   3-body flag 4:   same fall-off form, no Keq:  4; A0; n0; E0; Ai; ni; Ei; F; N;
!!   2-body flag 11:  k = A exp(B/T) (C/T + D P[Pa] + F)/100  (CRACMM NO + HO2 -> HNO3, exact)
!! Case conditions: T = 288.4 K, P = 880.0 mb, PhotoRates.in from the Williams TUV table.
!!
!! Format: "!! <label>: <CMAQ statement>" precedes each translated reaction.

!! 1: <1> NO2 = NO + O3P # 1.0/<NO2_06>;
NO2 => NO + O ; 0; 1;
!! 2: <2> O3P + O2 + M = O3 # 5.68e-34^-2.60;
!!   APPROXIMATION: ASP hard-wires O + O2 + M (flag 9): 5.6e-34 N2 / 6.0e-34 O2 (T/300)^-2.6 instead of the CMAQ coefficient; O(3P) is >99%% converted to O3 either way
O => O3 ; 9;
!! 3: <3> O3P + O3 = # 8.00e-12@2060;
O + O3 => M ; 8e-12; 0; -2060; 1;
!! 4: <4> O3P + NO = NO2 # 9.00e-32^-1.50&3.00e-11&0.60&1.0;
O + NO + M => NO2 + M ; 9e-32; 1.5; 3e-11; -0; 0.6;
!! 5: <5> O3P + NO2 = NO # 5.50e-12@-188;
O + NO2 => NO ; 5.5e-12; 0; 188; 1;
!! 6: <6> O3P + NO2 = NO3 # 2.50e-31^-1.80&2.20e-11^-0.70&0.60&1.0;
O + NO2 + M => NO3 + M ; 2.5e-31; 1.8; 2.2e-11; 0.7; 0.6;
!! 7: <7> O3 + NO = NO2 # 3.00e-12@1500;
O3 + NO => NO2 ; 3e-12; 0; -1500; 1;
!! 8: <8> O3 + NO2 = NO3 # 1.40e-13@2470;
O3 + NO2 => NO3 ; 1.4e-13; 0; -2470; 1;
!! 9: <9> NO + NO3 = 2*NO2 # 1.80e-11@-110;
NO + NO3 => 2 NO2 ; 1.8e-11; 0; 110; 1;
!! 10: <10> NO + NO + O2 = 2*NO2 # 3.30e-39@-530;
!!   NOTE: termolecular NO+NO+O2: 3-body rate flag 2 with [O2] = 0.2095 [M] (needs the common_asp flag-2 fix)
NO + NO + M => 2 NO2 + M ; 2; 6.9135e-40; 0; 530; 1;
!! 11: <11> NO2 + NO3 = N2O5 # 3.60e-30^-4.10&1.90e-12^0.20&0.35&1.33;
!!   NOTE: fall-off with F=0.35, N=1.33: ASP 3-body flag 4 (explicit N)
NO2 + NO3 + M => N2O5 + M ; 4; 3.6e-30; 4.1; -0; 1.9e-12; -0.2; -0; 0.35; 1.33;
!! 12: <12> N2O5 = NO2 + NO3 # 1.30e-03^-3.50@11000&9.70e+14^0.10@11080&0.35&1.33;
!!   NOTE: unimolecular fall-off: ASP 1-body flag 13 (explicit N, Keq = 1)
N2O5 => NO2 + NO3 ; 13; 0.0013; 3.5; -11000; 9.7e+14; -0.1; -11080; 0.35; 1.33; 1; 0;
!! 13: <13> N2O5 + H2O = 2*HNO3 # 1.00e-22;
N2O5 + H2O => 2 HNO3 ; 1e-22; 0; -0; 1;
